From 474d2f54fe0fb53d58495e6f770da20e77b70c05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:07:49 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 341/395] DWG and drawing PDF: texts kept, R2018 written, this
 version's converter, pages without a sheet

From the company's test of 0.7.6:
- A DWG written from a drawing lost every text: the DXF writer left out
  Draft texts. They are written as TEXT (one per line, the Draft text
  height). DWG is written as R2018 (dxf2dwg wrote the DXF's own version,
  R14; preference Mod/Draft DWGExportVersion).
- The converter that comes with this FreeCAD is used first; a path left in
  the settings by another version's bundle is replaced at start (an
  update kept using the old dxf2dwg).
- Texts and dimensions of DWG/DXF are read by default (Mod/Draft dxftext;
  a choice made in the preferences stays).
- A drawing page without its sheet (no template, or one without a file)
  is left out of --export-drawings with a warning; it stopped the export,
  or gave a blank PDF. A page without a template has an A4 landscape's
  size (asked for its size, it threw and the file did not open).

Tests: FreeCADCmd -t TestUnifiedFiles (DWG text round trip with a
converter), -t TestDrawingPdf, -t TestTechDrawApp

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
